      "extract": "Background Hepatitis B (HepB) is a major public health problem worldwide. Approximately 30% of the world's population, or about 1.8 billion persons, have serologic evidence of hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection. Of these, an estimated 350 million have chronic HBV infection and at least 500 000 chronically infected persons die each year from liver cancer and cirrhosis. HBV is second only to tobacco as a known human",
      "extractCut": true
    },
