      "words": 2228,
      "summary": {
        "text": "The main text of the English WHO note on hepatitis B immunization, setting routine infant vaccination as the top priority and recommending a birth dose within 24 hours where perinatal infection is common. It covers catch-up vaccination, monovalent versus combination formulations and three schedule options aligned with DTP doses. It also describes injection practice, equipment, cold chain, storage volumes, documents, training and budgeting. Some characters in the extracted text are garbled.",
        "status": "draft"
      },
